Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Meter: a button that shows or hides the plugin window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The plugin window (the dock) could be hidden by its × and brought back
only through Settings → Plugins. A puzzle button in the meter's header
now does both: it hides the dock as its × does, and shows it again with
the tabs it was hidden with (all of them if it never was). It is a
little brighter while the dock is shown (no colour of its own), follows
the dock when it is hidden or shown any other way (dock-status, sent by
plugins::dock::sync), and is absent while no plugin is in the dock.
While the meter is locked it stays clickable with the other header
buttons ("Locked: buttons stay clickable").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBQati3x8VviBbpY9juEWf
